          "id": 2,
          "options": {
            "content": "**Purpose.** One screen that answers *is the order journey healthy right now?* It shows symptoms (what customers feel) on top and saturation (likely causes) at the bottom.\n\n**Use it when** running a load test or the Christmas Rush demo, or when something looks wrong and you need to know where to look first.\n\n**How to read it**\n- Top row: demand and checkout. Success % and latency against the dashed 1.5s SLO line are the headline numbers.\n- Errors row: 5xx means a fault (SLO 1%). 4xx is usually business rejections: declines, stock-outs. Click a series to open that service on the **Service** dashboard.\n- Flow row: if dispatch stays below arrivals, the backlog grows. If event age passes the 2 min line, async processing is behind. Panel links (\u2197) drill down to **Dispatch & async flow** and **Checkout & payments**.\n- Saturation panels are causes, not symptoms. Click a pod to open it on **Pods & runtime**.\n- A dashed red line is an SLO. A panel with no data means that event hasn't happened yet.\n\n**Background:** [RED/USE best practices](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/dashboards/build-dashboards/best-practices/) \u00b7 [Hierarchy of needs](https://grafana.com/docs/learning-hub/intro-to-grafana-cloud/00-intro/02-hierarchy-of-needs) \u00b7 [Dashboards that matter](https://kindatechnical.com/microservices-architecture/building-observability-dashboards-that-matter.html) \u00b7 [ADR 0027](https://github.com/beckfordp/gluon/blob/main/docs/adr/0027-dashboard-architecture.md)",
            "mode": "markdown"
          },
          "repeatDirection": "h",
          "title": "",
          "transparent": false,
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "type": "row"
